Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: the empty Recents state is drawn at its final size

The Recents key shows Overview through a recents animation that starts
the view at the app window scale and settles to the overview scale. The
"No recent items" icon and text are drawn inside that scaled view, so they
appeared large and then shrank: two repaints, and the large one could be
left on the panel. They are now drawn with the view scale undone.

---
diff --git a/quickstep/src/com/android/quickstep/views/RecentsView.java b/quickstep/src/com/android/quickstep/views/RecentsView.java
--- a/quickstep/src/com/android/quickstep/views/RecentsView.java
+++ b/quickstep/src/com/android/quickstep/views/RecentsView.java
@@ -5784,6 +5784,12 @@
             int offset = (mEmptyIcon.getIntrinsicHeight() + mEmptyMessagePadding) / 2;
 
             canvas.save();
+            // Kompakt: undo the view's own scale, so the empty state is drawn at its final size
+            // from the first frame instead of shrinking into place (two repaints on e-ink).
+            if (getScaleX() > 0 && getScaleY() > 0) {
+                canvas.scale(1f / getScaleX(), 1f / getScaleY(),
+                        getScrollX() + getPivotX(), getPivotY());
+            }
             canvas.translate(getScrollX() + (mInsets.left - mInsets.right) / 2f,
                     (mInsets.top - mInsets.bottom) / 2f - offset);
             mEmptyIcon.draw(canvas);
-- 
